# Every text file checks out LF on every platform. The build and the checks hash and byte-compare checked-in text
# (the token schema pins, the ledgers, the db baseline, the content sha pins), so git's default Windows
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise turn a fresh clone into a hash mismatch, and a CRLF shell entrypoint copied
# into the image fails with `/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files stay CRLF: cmd.exe can misread labels and blocks in a batch file with LF line endings.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.avif  binary
*.woff2 binary
